## §A. Decomposition dossier — the Kummer K3 generator as a brick sequence

Kummer K3 = the smooth resolution of `T⁴/±1`. Elementary smooth topology (Benedetti arXiv:1907.10297
§20.2; Kirby–Taylor `Ω₄^{Spin}≅ℤ` generated by Kummer). Target = an inhabitant of
`PinPlusKTSpinSigmaStock.K3RealizingElement a` for the disclosed atom bundle `a`. The bricks:

**K0 — T⁴ base as a smooth closed 4-manifold.**  ← THIS MODULE, §B (DONE below).
`T⁴ = (S¹)⁴`, realized as `TorusFour = Circle × Circle × Circle × Circle` (four copies of Mathlib's
smooth circle `Circle = unit sphere ⊂ ℂ`, which carries `ChartedSpace`/`IsManifold (𝓡 1) ω`/`LieGroup`).
Machinery: Mathlib `Circle` smooth/Lie-group instances + the binary-product `ChartedSpace`/`IsManifold`
instances (`Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic` `instance prod`). Delivers charts, smoothness,
`T2Space`, `CompactSpace`, `Boundaryless`, `Nonempty`, `finrank = 4`.
Sub-wall (deferred, feeds K9): the product model is `(𝓡 1).prod (𝓡 1).prod …` on
`𝔼¹ × 𝔼¹ × 𝔼¹ × 𝔼¹`, NOT `𝓡 4` on `𝔼⁴`; the ultimate `StrMfd (spinEmptyData prov)` uses `I = 𝓡 4`.
Re-charting T⁴ onto `𝓡 4` (a model identification via the linear isometry `𝔼¹×𝔼¹×𝔼¹×𝔼¹ ≃ₗᵢ 𝔼⁴`)
is a K9 packaging brick.

**K1 — H₂(T⁴) ≅ ℤ⁶, intersection form = 3H.**  (Open; next after K0.)
The flat torus has `H₂(T⁴;ℤ) ≅ ℤ^(4 choose 2) = ℤ⁶`, cup form = 3 hyperbolic planes (`3H`, σ = 0,
even unimodular). Machinery: Mathlib group cohomology of `T⁴` is thin; the project's
`IntersectionMatrixInt.interMatrix` + `SphereWitnessTowerInt` S²×S² Gram template
(`SphereProdHTwoInt`/`SphereProdGramInt`) are the in-tree pattern for a concrete 4-manifold's
intersection form. Sub-wall: no Künneth/cup-product-on-a-product-basis in Mathlib — the `II(T⁴)=3H`
Gram identity is a disclosed geometric atom (same posture as the S²×S² `SphereProdGramPin`).

**K2 — the involution τ(w) = −w on T⁴.**  (Open.)
On `(S¹)⁴`, `τ = ` complex-conjugation on each factor (`z ↦ z̄`, a `Circle` anti-automorphism / the
group inverse composed with nothing — actually `z ↦ z⁻¹ = z̄` on the unit circle). Smooth involution,
`τ² = id`. Machinery: `Circle` group inverse is smooth (`LieGroup`), product of smooth maps
(`ContMDiff.prod_map`). Sub-wall: proving `τ` smooth as an `𝓡 4`-manifold self-map and identifying its
fixed set (below).

**K3 — the 16 fixed points of τ.**  (Open.)
`Fix(τ) = (½ℤ/ℤ)⁴`: on each `S¹` factor `z̄ = z ⟺ z = ±1`, so `Fix = {±1}⁴`, exactly `2⁴ = 16` points.
Machinery: `Circle` elements `1` and `-1` (= the two real points); `Finset`/`Fintype` cardinality on
`(Fin 2)⁴`. Sub-wall: identifying `{z : Circle | z⁻¹ = z} = {1, -1}` (a `Circle`-membership computation)
and transporting to the product.

**⚠ ROUTE SUPERSEDED (lead design pass 2026-07-20): K4–K6 as stated below are replaced by ROUTE B**
(excise-first / free-quotient / boundary-weld — the singular orbifold carrier is never built; van Kampen
