neighborhoods (from K3's finite fixed set); `SingularSurgeryManifold` connect/glue operations.
Sub-wall: bookkeeping 16 simultaneous disjoint gluings; establishing simple-connectivity of the result
(van Kampen — Mathlib `π₁` support is thin).

**K7 — H₂(Kummer) ≅ ℤ²².**  (Open.)
`b₂ = 22`: from `H₂(T⁴/τ-smooth-part)` (the τ-invariant part of `H₂(T⁴)=ℤ⁶`, contributing rank 6) plus
the 16 exceptional `(−2)`-spheres (rank 16); `6 + 16 = 22`. Machinery: Mayer–Vietoris over the 16
gluings; the S²×S²/`SphereWitnessTowerInt` rank-computation template; `IntH2Basis`. Sub-wall: the MV /
invariant-subspace rank accounting as an in-tree homology computation (no manifold H_* in Mathlib —
disclosed-atom posture, cf. K1).

**K8 — intersection form = 2(−E₈) ⊕ 3H (σ = −16).**  (Open — the payoff.)
The 16 `(−2)`-spheres contribute `2·(−E₈)` (the E₈ plumbing pattern from the resolution graph), the
descended `T⁴` part contributes `3H`. This is *exactly* the already-proven `SpinSigmaGenerator.k3Form`.
Machinery: `k3Form`, `k3Form_isEvenUnimodular`, `k3Form_latticeSig = −16` (DONE, in-tree);
`IntersectionMatrixInt.interMatrix`; `HyperbolicNormalForm.IntCongr` for the `IntCongr … k3Form`
target. Sub-wall: the geometric Gram identity `II(Kummer) ≅ k3Form` — a disclosed atom (Milnor–Husemoller
uniqueness of the rank-22 even unimodular σ=−16 form pins the lattice; the *manifold*'s realizing it is
the geometric input), the direct analogue of the S²×S² `SphereProdGramPin`.

**K9 — spin structure + `StrMfd` packaging on `𝓡 4`.**  (Open — packaging.)
Kummer K3 is spin (its form is even ⟹ `w₂ = 0`). Package as `SingularManifold X 4 (𝓡 4)` → choose the
spin tangential structure (`spinEmptyData prov`'s `Mfd`) → `StrMfd (spinEmptyData prov)`. Resolves the
K0 sub-wall (re-chart onto `𝓡 4`). Machinery: `TangentialDataBordism.StrMfd`,
`PinPlusKTSpinForgetPhi.spinEmptyData`, the S⁴/`sphereProdSM`/`rp4SM` StrMfd-witness templates.
Sub-wall: constructing the `SingularManifold` bundle on `𝓡 4` and inhabiting the spin `Mfd` slot.

**K10 — `SpinSigmaAtomPkg` (orient / B / pd) + `K3RealizingElement`.**  (Open — the capstone.)
Supply the per-element E1 package: integral orientation (`IntOrientation`, from H₄(K3)≅ℤ), the rank-22
`IntH2Basis` (K7), integral Poincaré duality (`IntPoincareDuality`, unimodularity from K8). Assemble
`K3RealizingElement a` with `hrank : (a.B g).rank = 22` (K7) and `hk3 : IntCongr (interMatrix …) k3Form`
(K8). Machinery: `PinPlusKTSpinSigmaStock` package templates (S⁴ `sphere4IntOrientation`/
`sphere4IntPoincareDuality`; S²×S² Gram-pin discharge). Sub-wall: the `IntOrientation.redCompat` mod-2
comparison (the S²×S² arc's noted per-element-vs-functional gap) at the K3 orientation.

**Critical-path summary.** K0 (done) → K1 → {K2→K3→K4→K5→K6} → K7 → K8 → K9 → K10. The recurring
disclosed-atom pattern (K1, K7, K8: "the manifold's H_*/cup form equals the computed lattice") mirrors
